---
import ArrowIcon from '../components/ArrowIcon.astro';
import SupportShell from '../components/SupportShell.astro';
import ActionIcon from '../components/ActionIcon.astro';
const cases=[['Print a page for yourself or your family','Free personal use'],['Use pages in a non-commercial classroom or learning activity','Free educational use'],['Post a photo of your completed coloring with JotColoring credit','Permitted with credit'],['Sell products, paid publications or coloring packs','Written permission first'],['Use an illustration in advertising, an app or a business project','Written permission first'],['Repost blank files, build a download bundle or resell the collection','Permission required']];
---
<SupportShell title="Artwork license" description="Print it. Color it. Enjoy it. Know what is free to use and when to ask for permission." kind="license" eyebrow="A LITTLE CREATIVITY. CLEAR PERMISSION.">
 <div slot="hero" class="support-hero-meta"><span>Personal use: free</span><span>Non-commercial education: free</span><span>Commercial use: ask first</span></div>
 <div class="support-card-grid"><section class="support-card"><ActionIcon name="heart"/><h2>Make time for color.</h2><p>Download, print and color collection pages for yourself, your family and your own creative enjoyment. Keep the small JotColoring™ credit on the supplied page.</p></section><section class="support-card"><ActionIcon name="pdf"/><h2>Bring it to class.</h2><p>Use pages for non-commercial teaching, classroom activities and learning at home. A sale, paid publication or commercial product needs separate permission.</p></section><section class="support-card"><ActionIcon name="brush"/><h2>Have a business idea?</h2><p>Tell us which image you want and how you will use it. Commercial permission must be confirmed in writing before you publish or sell.</p><a href="/licensing/">Request a license<ArrowIcon kind="right" size={18}/></a></section></div>
 <div class="support-section-heading"><p class="support-kicker">REAL-LIFE EXAMPLES</p><h2>Can I use it for this?</h2><p>These examples help you find the right next step. If a use is unclear, ask before distributing it.</p></div>
 <div class="support-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Artwork usage examples; scroll horizontally on small screens"><table class="support-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Your idea</th><th scope="col">Permission</th></tr></thead><tbody>{cases.map(([idea,permission],index)=><tr><td>{idea}</td><td><span class={index<3?'support-ok':'support-permission'}>{permission}</span></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
 <div class="support-prose-layout"><aside class="support-toc"><h2>THE DETAILS</h2><nav aria-label="License sections"><a href="#credit">Sharing & credit</a><a href="#blank-files">Blank files & redistribution</a><a href="#own-work">Your uploads & colors</a><a href="#rights">Rights we can grant</a><a href="#permission">Written permission</a></nav></aside><article class="support-prose">
 <section id="credit"><h2>Sharing your colorful version</h2><p>You may share a photo or image of your completed personal coloring with credit to JotColoring. Keep the JotColoring™ credit on copies of a supplied collection page. A link to the original coloring page helps others find their own copy.</p><p>This sharing permission does not allow selling the artwork, making merchandise or granting a commercial license to someone else. A social post showing your coloring and a product for sale are different uses.</p></section>
 <section id="blank-files"><h2>Keep the collection in its creative home</h2><p>Please link people to the original JotColoring page instead of hosting the uncolored PDF or image yourself. Republishing blank collection files, building a download library, selling files or bundling the collection requires written permission.</p><p>Do not remove the brand credit from a supplied page or imply that JotColoring has endorsed your project. JotColoring™ is our brand credit; the symbol is not a claim of registered trademark status.</p></section>
 <section id="own-work"><h2>Your uploads and your coloring</h2><p>You keep the rights you hold in your own photos, images and other uploaded material. Only upload material you have permission to use. Your choice of colors does not remove the underlying conditions on a collection illustration.</p><p>Studio saves stay on your device unless you choose to share them. Exporting a picture or an editable backup does not change the artwork’s license.</p></section>
 <section id="rights"><h2>What this permission covers</h2><p>The collection includes AI-assisted illustrations prepared for JotColoring. These permissions cover rights JotColoring can grant. They do not promise exclusive rights, copyright protection for every AI-assisted element, or clearance of third-party brands, likenesses or other protected subjects.</p><p>Downloading a page does not transfer ownership. Commercial suitability and the rights available for a particular project must be reviewed before written permission is issued.</p></section>
 <section id="permission"><h2>Ask once, with the useful details</h2><p>Send the page URL, intended use, audience, quantity, distribution and duration to <a href="/contact/?topic=licensing#message">our contact form</a>. We will review the request and confirm the available rights and terms. A request alone is not an issued license.</p><div class="support-actions"><a class="support-button" href="/licensing/">Prepare a license request<ArrowIcon kind="right" size={18}/></a><a class="support-button secondary" href="/faq/?topic=permissions">Licensing questions<ArrowIcon kind="right" size={18}/></a></div></section>
 <div class="support-note"><strong>Effective October 29, 2026</strong><p>Read this page alongside our <a href="/terms/">Terms of use</a>. For a use outside the free permission, obtain written approval before publishing.</p></div></article></div>
</SupportShell>
